#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:2
msgid "Writing a ``rosidl::Buffer`` backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:4
msgid ""
"**Goal:** Learn how to implement and package a new ``rosidl::Buffer`` "
"backend plugin so that a vendor-specific memory domain (GPU, shared memory, "
"accelerator memory, ...) can back ``uint8[]`` fields of ROS 2 messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:8
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Advanced"
msgstr "**教學等級：** 進階"

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:10
msgid "**Time:** 60+ minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:13
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr "目次表"

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:16
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:18
msgid ""
":doc:`rosidl::Buffer backends <About-Buffer-Backends>` let vendors transport "
"the bytes of a ``uint8[]`` message field through ROS 2 pub/sub with as few "
"copies as their memory technology permits. A backend is a ``pluginlib`` "
"plugin that implements the ``rosidl::BufferBackend`` interface from the "
"``rosidl_buffer_backend`` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:25
msgid ""
"This guide shows how to build such a plugin, end to end. It uses a "
"hypothetical ``mydev`` backend in the prose (for a vendor device memory "
"domain) and refers to the real CUDA backend, the ``torch_conversions`` "
"helper library, and the demo backend in the reference links for concrete "
"code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:30
msgid ""
"This guide is intended as a starting point; the existing reference backends "
"go into much more detail than is practical to reproduce here. The core "
"contract, however, is small: once your plugin can answer the six "
"``BufferBackend`` virtuals correctly for a single message type, everything "
"else is polish."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:37
msgid "When **not** to write a backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:39
msgid ""
"A backend is the right tool when you want to change the *memory domain* of "
"variable-length primitive array fields. If your goal is to reduce copies "
"within CPU memory, you are almost certainly looking for :doc:`intra-process "
"communication </ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/intra-process/Intra-"
"Process-Communication>` or :doc:`loaned messages <../../../client-libraries/"
"Working-with-Client-Libraries/Configure-ZeroCopy-loaned-messages>` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:43
msgid "Reference implementations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:45
msgid ""
"Two open-source backends and one user-level tensor library are good reading. "
"All are small enough to read in full:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:48
msgid ""
"``cuda_buffer_backend``: a realistic CUDA backend built on CUDA VMM and CUDA "
"IPC, with intra-process, inter-process same-host, and CPU-fallback paths. "
"See `ros2/rosidl_buffer_backends <https://github.com/ros2/"
"rosidl_buffer_backends>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:52
msgid ""
"``torch_conversions``: a header-only user library, not a backend plugin. It "
"converts between ``tensor_msgs/msg/ExperimentalTensor`` and ``at::Tensor``. "
"The tensor message's ``uint8[] data`` field is transported by an ordinary "
"buffer backend such as ``cuda`` or ``cpu``. Same repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:59
msgid "The ``BufferBackend`` interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:61
msgid ""
"The plugin interface is declared in `rosidl_buffer_backend/buffer_backend."
"hpp <https://github.com/ros2/rosidl/blob/rolling/rosidl_buffer_backend/"
"include/rosidl_buffer_backend/buffer_backend.hpp>`__. It has six methods you "
"will commonly override, plus a descriptor-size constant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:67
msgid ""
"namespace rosidl\n"
"{\n"
"\n"
"inline constexpr size_t kMaxBufferDescriptorSize = 4096;\n"
"\n"
"class BufferBackend\n"
"{\n"
"public:\n"
"  virtual ~BufferBackend() = default;\n"
"\n"
"  // Identity\n"
"  virtual std::string get_backend_type() const = 0;\n"
"  virtual std::string get_backend_metadata() const { return \"\"; }\n"
"\n"
"  // Descriptor type support and construction\n"
"  virtual const rosidl_message_type_support_t *\n"
"  get_descriptor_type_support() const = 0;\n"
"  virtual std::shared_ptr<void> create_empty_descriptor() const = 0;\n"
"  virtual std::shared_ptr<void> create_descriptor_with_endpoint(\n"
"    const void * impl,\n"
"    const rmw_topic_endpoint_info_t & endpoint_info) const = 0;\n"
"  virtual std::unique_ptr<void, void (*)(void *)>\n"
"  from_descriptor_with_endpoint(\n"
"    const void * descriptor,\n"
"    const rmw_topic_endpoint_info_t & endpoint_info) const = 0;\n"
"\n"
"  // Discovery hooks (optional to override)\n"
"  virtual void on_creating_endpoint(\n"
"    const rmw_topic_endpoint_info_t & endpoint_info) const;\n"
"  virtual std::pair<bool, std::vector<std::set<uint32_t>>>\n"
"  on_discovering_endpoint(\n"
"    const rmw_topic_endpoint_info_t & endpoint_info,\n"
"    const std::vector<rmw_topic_endpoint_info_t> & existing_endpoints,\n"
"    const std::unordered_map<std::string, std::string> & "
"endpoint_supported_backends);\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"}  // namespace rosidl"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:108
msgid "Anatomy of a backend package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:110
msgid ""
"A complete backend is usually split across three or four ROS 2 packages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:112
msgid ""
"**Core memory-domain library** (e.g. ``mydev_buffer``): the non-plugin code "
"-- custom allocator, ``BufferImplBase<T>`` subclass, IPC manager, RAII "
"handles. This is where most of the vendor's engineering lives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:116
msgid ""
"**Descriptor message package** (e.g. ``mydev_buffer_backend_msgs``): a "
"normal ROS 2 ``.msg`` that describes how to reconstruct the buffer on the "
"receiving side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:119
msgid ""
"**Backend plugin package** (e.g. ``mydev_buffer_backend``): a thin shared "
"library that implements ``rosidl::BufferBackend`` and is registered via "
"``pluginlib``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:122
msgid ""
"**User-facing API header** (optional, usually shipped inside the core "
"library): helpers like ``allocate_buffer``, ``from_output_buffer``, "
"``from_input_buffer``, and ``to_buffer`` that application authors use to "
"produce and consume backend-native data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:128
msgid "Step 1: Design the descriptor message"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:130
msgid ""
"The descriptor is the only thing that actually travels over the wire. It "
"must contain everything the receiving endpoint needs to reconstruct a buffer "
"whose size and contents match the publisher's buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:134
msgid "Two important constraints:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:136
msgid ""
"The serialized descriptor must be no larger than ``rosidl::"
"kMaxBufferDescriptorSize`` bytes (4096). The RMW plans its serialization "
"buffers around this bound."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:139
msgid ""
"The descriptor package must be a plain ``rosidl_default_generators`` message "
"package so that the generic ``rosidl_typesupport_cpp::"
"get_message_type_support_handle<T>()`` returns an aggregate handle that "
"contains the FastRTPS C++ sub-handle. (Today that sub-handle is the one the "
"RMW layer extracts; see :ref:`writing-buffer-backend_type-support`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:146
msgid ""
"A descriptor typically carries either a small reference that the receiving "
"side uses to re-attach to the payload, a serialized copy of the payload for "
"the CPU-fallback case, or both. The exact re-attachment mechanism is backend-"
"specific. For example, a simplified device-IPC descriptor might look like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:150
msgid ""
"# mydev_buffer_backend_msgs/msg/MyDevBufferDescriptor.msg\n"
"uint64 size                       # allocation size in bytes\n"
"int32  device_id                  # producing device\n"
"\n"
"# IPC path (preferred)\n"
"bool   use_ipc\n"
"string ipc_socket_path\n"
"uint32 ipc_block_id\n"
"uint64 ipc_uid                    # unique id for staleness detection\n"
"\n"
"# CPU fallback (empty when IPC is used)\n"
"uint8[] serialized_data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:165
msgid ""
"The real CUDA backend (``cuda_buffer_backend_msgs/CudaBufferDescriptor."
"msg``) illustrates the device-IPC shape: the descriptor carries the "
"publisher process id, block id, socket path, and synchronization metadata "
"needed to import a CUDA VMM block. The exported file descriptor itself is "
"passed out-of-band over the Unix-domain socket named by the descriptor. If "
"the backend cannot serve a peer through CUDA IPC, it returns ``nullptr`` so "
"that peer receives the field through CPU fallback instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:175
msgid "Step 2: Implement ``BufferImplBase<T>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:177
msgid ""
"``BufferImplBase<T>`` is the pimpl that lives inside ``rosidl::Buffer<T>``. "
"Its interface is intentionally minimal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:180
msgid ""
"template<typename T>\n"
"class BufferImplBase\n"
"{\n"
"public:\n"
"  virtual ~BufferImplBase() = default;\n"
"  virtual std::string get_backend_type() const = 0;\n"
"  virtual size_t size() const = 0;\n"
"  virtual std::unique_ptr<BufferImplBase<T>> to_cpu() const = 0;\n"
"  virtual std::unique_ptr<BufferImplBase<T>> clone() const = 0;\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:193
msgid ""
"``get_backend_type()`` must return the same short name your plugin's XML "
"declares (``\"cuda\"``, ``\"mydev\"``, ...)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:195
msgid ""
"``size()`` returns the element count (not byte count, unless ``T`` is "
"``uint8_t``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:197
msgid ""
"``to_cpu()`` is the escape hatch used by ``Buffer<T>::to_vector()`` when a "
"consumer explicitly wants CPU memory; it must return a populated "
"``CpuBufferImpl<T>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:200
msgid ""
"``clone()`` produces a deep copy of ``*this``; it is used by ``Buffer<T>``'s "
"copy constructor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:203
msgid ""
"Beyond those four required methods, your implementation will usually hold "
"all of your backend's state: device pointers, IPC handles, cached streams, "
"staleness counters, and so on. The plugin side of the interface then talks "
"to this state through ``dynamic_cast`` to your concrete type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:210
msgid "Step 3: Implement ``BufferBackend``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:215
msgid "Identity and descriptor type support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:217
msgid ""
"``get_backend_type()`` returns the short name. "
"``get_descriptor_type_support()`` should return the **generic** aggregate "
"type support handle for your descriptor, not a specific typesupport "
"library's handle:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:222
msgid ""
"const rosidl_message_type_support_t *\n"
"MyDevBufferBackend::get_descriptor_type_support() const\n"
"{\n"
"  return rosidl_typesupport_cpp::get_message_type_support_handle<\n"
"    mydev_buffer_backend_msgs::msg::MyDevBufferDescriptor>();\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:231
msgid ""
"This keeps the plugin RMW-agnostic. Current RMW integrations resolve the "
"aggregate to ``rosidl_typesupport_fastrtps_cpp`` at runtime, so any standard "
"``rosidl_default_generators`` message package will work out of the box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:237
msgid "``create_descriptor_with_endpoint`` / ``from_descriptor_with_endpoint``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:239
msgid "These are the two hot-path methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:241
msgid ""
"``create_descriptor_with_endpoint`` is called on the publisher side once per "
"matched remote endpoint. It receives a type-erased non-owning pointer to a "
"``BufferImplBase<uint8_t>`` and the peer's ``rmw_topic_endpoint_info_t``. "
"Return a filled-in descriptor for that peer, or ``nullptr`` to tell the RMW "
"*\"I cannot serve this peer with my backend; please fall back to CPU "
"serialization.\"*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:249
msgid "Returning ``nullptr`` is a first-class signal. Use it whenever:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:252
msgid ""
"the peer does not support your backend (check "
"``endpoint_supported_backends`` during discovery and cache the answer);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:254
msgid ""
"the hardware or environment cannot serve this pair (different device, "
"different host, IPC disabled, ...);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:256
msgid "any other reason a non-CPU path is not available for *this* peer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:258
msgid ""
"``from_descriptor_with_endpoint`` is the inverse, invoked on the subscriber "
"side. It must produce a ``std::unique_ptr<void, void (*)(void *)>`` owning a "
"freshly-constructed ``BufferImplBase<T>``. The custom deleter is "
"**required** because the plugin may be unloaded independently of the rest of "
"the process; the deleter ensures destruction happens inside the correct "
"shared library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:266
msgid "A typical deleter looks like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:268
msgid ""
"auto impl = std::make_unique<MyDevBufferImpl<uint8_t>>(...);\n"
"return {impl.release(), [](void * p) {\n"
"    delete static_cast<rosidl::BufferImplBase<uint8_t> *>(p);\n"
"  }};"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:276
msgid "Discovery hooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:278
msgid ""
"``on_creating_endpoint`` lets your backend learn about local publishers and "
"subscriptions as they are created; this is usually where IPC managers "
"register themselves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:282
msgid ""
"``on_discovering_endpoint`` is the compatibility negotiation step. It "
"returns a ``std::pair<bool, std::vector<std::set<uint32_t>>>``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:285
msgid ""
"The ``bool`` tells the RMW whether this peer is served by the backend at "
"all. Returning ``false`` permanently routes this peer to CPU serialization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:288
msgid ""
"The ``std::vector<std::set<uint32_t>>`` is for backends that need to group "
"endpoints (e.g. which subscribers share the same device and can use the same "
"IPC handle). Most backends leave this empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:293
msgid ""
"The ``endpoint_supported_backends`` argument is a map from the peer's "
"advertised backend names to their metadata strings. A correct backend "
"**must** check that its own name is in this map before declaring the peer "
"compatible; otherwise a publisher will waste descriptor work on a "
"subscription that cannot consume it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:299
msgid "Simplified example from the CUDA backend:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:301
msgid ""
"std::pair<bool, std::vector<std::set<uint32_t>>>\n"
"CudaBufferBackend::on_discovering_endpoint(\n"
"  const rmw_topic_endpoint_info_t & /*endpoint_info*/,\n"
"  const std::vector<rmw_topic_endpoint_info_t> & /*existing_endpoints*/,\n"
"  const std::unordered_map<std::string, std::string> & "
"endpoint_supported_backends)\n"
"{\n"
"  if (endpoint_supported_backends.find(\"cuda\") ==\n"
"      endpoint_supported_backends.end())\n"
"  {\n"
"    return {false, {}};\n"
"  }\n"
"\n"
"  // The full implementation also checks VMM IPC support, endpoint\n"
"  // locality, device id, and user id before returning true.\n"
"  return {true, {}};\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:321
msgid "Step 4: Register the plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:323
msgid "Add a ``pluginlib`` XML file that declares your backend class:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:325
msgid ""
"<!-- mydev_buffer_backend/mydev_buffer_plugin.xml -->\n"
"<library path=\"mydev_buffer_backend\">\n"
"  <class name=\"mydev\"\n"
"         type=\"mydev_buffer_backend::MyDevBufferBackend\"\n"
"         base_class_type=\"rosidl::BufferBackend\">\n"
"    <description>Example backend for the mydev memory domain.</description>\n"
"  </class>\n"
"</library>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:336
msgid ""
"The ``name`` attribute is the short name that users put into "
"``acceptable_buffer_backends`` (see :doc:`Using-Buffer-Backends`) and that "
"your ``get_backend_type()`` must return."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:341
msgid "Export it from ``CMakeLists.txt``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:343
msgid ""
"pluginlib_export_plugin_description_file(\n"
"  rosidl_buffer_backend mydev_buffer_plugin.xml)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:348
msgid "and install it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:350
msgid ""
"install(\n"
"  FILES mydev_buffer_plugin.xml\n"
"  DESTINATION share/${PROJECT_NAME}\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:357
msgid "And register the class in your plugin source file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:359
msgid ""
"#include <pluginlib/class_list_macros.hpp>\n"
"#include \"mydev_buffer_backend/mydev_buffer_backend.hpp\"\n"
"\n"
"PLUGINLIB_EXPORT_CLASS(\n"
"  mydev_buffer_backend::MyDevBufferBackend,\n"
"  rosidl::BufferBackend)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:369
msgid "Step 5: Package and build system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:372
msgid "``package.xml`` for the plugin package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:374
msgid ""
"<package format=\"3\">\n"
"  <name>mydev_buffer_backend</name>\n"
