#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:460
msgid "Step 6: Design a user-facing API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:462
msgid ""
"Application authors do not typically construct ``BufferImplBase`` subclasses "
"by hand; they go through a user-facing API header shipped by the backend. A "
"minimal API usually provides three operations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:466
msgid ""
"**Allocate a buffer** whose storage is already backed by your backend's "
"memory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:469
msgid "rosidl::Buffer<uint8_t> allocate_buffer(std::size_t byte_count);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:473
msgid ""
"**Obtain a writable handle** to a backend-backed buffer so the caller can "
"produce data in place (e.g. launch a kernel writing into the device pointer):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:477
msgid "WriteHandle from_output_buffer(rosidl::Buffer<uint8_t> & buffer, ...);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:481
msgid ""
"**Obtain a readable handle** on the subscriber side, synchronised with "
"whatever the publisher's write did (e.g. waiting on a shared event):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:484
msgid ""
"ReadHandle from_input_buffer(const rosidl::Buffer<uint8_t> & buffer, ...);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:488
msgid "Typical auxiliary considerations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:490
msgid ""
"**Auto-promotion**: if a caller hands your backend a buffer that happens to "
"live in some other backend (CPU, another device backend, ...), a helpful "
"pattern is to allocate a new buffer in *your* domain and copy into it "
"transparently, keeping ownership via a ``get_promoted_buffer()`` getter on "
"the returned handle. The CUDA backend does this for CPU-to-CUDA inputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:496
msgid ""
"**Synchronisation**: if your backend is asynchronous (streams, events, "
"queues), encode the synchronisation policy into your handle types rather "
"than on the free functions. RAII on destruction makes correct use the "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:502
msgid "Higher-level libraries on top of backends"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:504
msgid ""
"Do not write a new backend just to add application-level metadata such as "
"tensor shape, point-cloud fields, or image color-space information. Those "
"semantics fit better in a normal ROS 2 message whose payload field is a "
"``uint8[]`` and therefore a ``rosidl::Buffer<uint8_t>`` in generated C++ "
"code. The message can then ride on whichever storage backend is negotiated "
"for that field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:511
msgid "The tensor packages in ``rosidl_buffer_backends`` follow this model:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:513
msgid ""
"``tensor_msgs/msg/ExperimentalTensor`` stores DLPack-aligned dtype, shape, "
"stride, and byte-offset metadata plus a ``uint8[] data`` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:515
msgid ""
"``torch_conversions`` converts between that message and ``at::Tensor``. It "
"allocates CUDA-backed ``data`` when requested and available, otherwise it "
"uses CPU storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:518
msgid ""
"Subscribers opt in to the underlying storage backend (for example "
"``acceptable_buffer_backends = \"cuda\"`` or ``\"any\"``), not to a separate "
"tensor backend name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:522
msgid ""
"This keeps the backend ecosystem focused on memory transport while allowing "
"ordinary user libraries to add richer programming models above it. See :doc:"
"`Writing-a-Buffer-Compatible-Conversions-Package` for a dedicated guide to "
"creating ``*_conversions`` packages on top of buffer-backed message fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:529
msgid "Testing"
msgstr "測試"

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:531
msgid ""
"The most useful tests for a backend are launch tests that exercise real pub/"
"sub topologies. The reference CUDA backend ships a representative set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:535
msgid "intra-process (publisher and subscriber in the same process);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:536
msgid "inter-process on the same host;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:537
msgid "mixed intra/inter-process (one publisher, multiple subscribers);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:538
msgid "multi-publisher (several producers into one topic);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:539
msgid ""
"CPU fallback (subscriber that does not advertise the backend must still "
"receive correct bytes);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:541
msgid ""
"\"mixed / no duplicate\" (a subscription that accepts both the backend and "
"CPU must not observe duplicated messages)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Writing-a-Buffer-Backend.rst:544
msgid "See ``cuda_buffer_backend/test/`` for the full set."
msgstr ""

